window.docContents[109].resolve({"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.PqxdhModelLink/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___PqxdhModelLink":{"contents":"Paper › LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E › PqxdhModelLink.leanTier 1 · statement file\n\nTier 1 · statement file used by the computational proof 3 headline theorems depend on it 155 lines trust banner B1, trusted: the statement source ↗Read in full. A statement file: its definitions say what the headline theorems claim (games, adversaries, bounds). Proofs are cut after := and shown as ⋯; Lean checks them.\n\nDeclarations on this page (10)def u8Vecdef vecU8def beWorddef sha256StateOfdef sha512StateOfdef sha256StateBytesdef sha512StateBytesBEstructure UnreachedPqxdhPrimitivesdef blockLevelPrimsdef modelPrims\n\n\n\nBridge from End-to-End Primitives to SignalPqxdh.Primitives (modelPrims)Trusted: the statement. Instantiates SignalPqxdh.Primitives (SignalPqxdh/Model.lean) from the session primitives C : Crypto, the PQXDH hooks Q : PqxdhPrims, and the unreached model operations X : UnreachedPqxdhPrimitives:* Block-level primitives (blockLevelPrims) adapt byte and endianness encodings (big-endian SHA words, little-endian AES keys/blocks, clamped X25519 scalars, and length-checked Kyber inputs).* Derived primitives (modelPrims) use the pure model's reference constructions (sha512Ref, xeddsaVerifyRef, isCanonicalRef, hkdfDerive96Ref, chain KDFs, and AEAD).* Unused SPQR fields in SignalPqxdh.Primitives are stubs; V1 SPQR runs in the session model (pqxdhSpqrSession, DEV-PQ3).\n\n\n\nByte conversions\n\ndef u8VecL39–40 ↗#A model byte string (List UInt8) as a machine vector of n bytes: fitVec n ∘ ofU8.\n\ndef vecU8L42–43 ↗#A machine vector as a model byte string.\n\ndef beWordL45–48 ↗#The k-th big-endian w-bit word of bs (bytes k·(w/8) .. (k+1)·(w/8) − 1, missing bytes zero).\n\ndef sha256StateOfL50–52 ↗#A 32-byte SHA-256 chaining state (FIPS 180-4's H as big-endian bytes) as eight words.\n\ndef sha512StateOfL54–56 ↗#A 64-byte SHA-512 chaining state as eight words.\n\ndef sha256StateBytesL58–59 ↗#A SHA-256 chaining state as its 32 big-endian bytes.\n\ndef sha512StateBytesBEL61–62 ↗#A SHA-512 chaining state as its 64 big-endian bytes.\n\nThe fields with no binary counterpart\n\nstructure UnreachedPqxdhPrimitivesL66–83 ↗#The model's primitives that no handshake entry reaches: XEdDSA public-key derivation and signing, scalar multiplication and addition mod ℓ, Kyber key generation, and the security model's cofactor projection and DDH predicate. Universally quantified in the statement.\n\nThe primitives\n\ndef blockLevelPrimsL87–137 ↗#The block-level primitives at (X, W); the derived fields are placeholders, replaced in modelPrims. kemEncaps and kemDecaps reject inputs whose byte length differs from SignalPqxdh.kyberPkLen and SignalPqxdh.kyberCtLen, matching PublicKey and Ciphertext deserialization in rust/protocol/src/kem.rs.\n\ndef modelPrimsL139–156 ↗#The PQXDH model's primitives at (X, W): blockLevelPrims with every derived field replaced by the model's reference construction over the block-level fields.\n\n\n\n","context":"AlphaProof Code: Verifying Signal’s Security at the Machine-Code Level","header":"LibsignalBinary/Specifications/LibsignalE2E/PqxdhModelLink.lean","id":"/Tier-1___-statements/Statement-files-_LPAR_T_RPAR_/LibsignalBinary.Specifications.LibsignalE2E.PqxdhModelLink/#file-LibsignalBinary___Specifications___LibsignalE2E___PqxdhModelLink"}});